ly song)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" It contains references to artists from Cleveland, as well as to the life in the state of Ohio.","title":"Till I Die (Machine Gun Kelly song)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The song received positive reviews, with critics praising MGK's lyrical ability and inert references to Cleveland, describing the song as a "perfect trap anthem".","title":"Till I Die (Machine Gun Kelly song)"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" The song was produced by J.U.S.T.I.C.E. League when the song was recorded in 2014, and the group also handled the distribution of the song.","title":"Till I Die (Machine Gun Kelly song)"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" A new version of the song is also featured on the soundtrack for "NBA 2K16".","title":"Till I Die (Machine Gun Kelly song)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Girls' Generation (Hangul: 소녀시대; RR: "Sonyeo Sidae") is a Korean song sung by several artists.","title":"Girls' Generation (song)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The song was originally sung by Lee Seung-chul in 1989, released on his self-titled album "Lee Seung-chul: Part 2" (Korean: 이승철 1집 Part 2).","title":"Girls' Generation (song)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" It was covered by Maya in 2005 and girl group Girls' Generation in 2007, whose band name is derived from the song's.","title":"Girls' Generation (song)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" also performed the song at Superstar K in 2009 and it was released on "" which contains songs by the first Superstar K Top 10.","title":"Girls' Generation (song)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":""I Miss You" is a song by American rock band Blink-182, released on February 9, 2004 as the second single from the group's fifth studio album, "Blink-182" (2003).","title":"I Miss You (Blink-182 song)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Co-written by guitarist Tom DeLonge and bassist Mark Hoppus, they employed a method of writing separately and bringing their two verses together later.","title":"I Miss You (Blink-182 song)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The song, produced entirely acoustic, features an acoustic electric bass, a cello, and a brushstroked drum loop.","title":"I Miss You (Blink-182 song)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The song was inspired by The Cure song "The Love Cats" and contains references to "The Nightmare Before Christmas" (1993).","title":"I Miss You (Blink-182 song)"}],"peer_messages":[" member of the H Band with Marillion's lead singer Steve Hogarth and is involved in the writing of the second H Band album.","title":"Aziz Ibrahim"}
